PROJECT ORIGIN

The initial pipeline was developed while following Abdullah Tarek's
"Build an AI/ML Tennis Analysis System" tutorial:

https://github.com/abdullahtarek/tennis_analysis
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L23oIHZE14w

This attribution applies to the tutorial-based starting point, not to the
subsequent project-specific work listed below.

PROJECT-SPECIFIC WORK

I extended the tutorial baseline through guided development and learning,
including:

- a reusable and validated end-to-end pipeline;
- content-addressed detection caching;
- source-FPS handling and frame-rate-normalized shot detection;
- structured per-frame CSV statistics;
- a manually annotated, video-separated shot-event benchmark;
- one-to-one temporal event evaluation with block-bootstrap confidence
  intervals and a multi-clip runner;
- an alternating-swing shot detector evaluated with a pre-registered
  leave-one-clip-out protocol;
- development-set error analysis and a measured F1 improvement;
- automated tests and GitHub Actions;
- player-role synchronization and corrected statistics;
- a redesigned mini court, statistics dashboard, and visual demo;
- repository-history cleanup and reproducibility documentation.

